# Administrative workspace preview

Import AdminShell from "../src/admin_shell.lg".

The Page mounts the presentation shell with the board policy's current outcomes
as explicit inputs: six phases, and Closed refusing ordinary work. The policy
itself is tested in its import-free leaves, which a Page must not import; the
production root in src/admin_app.lg binds those leaves to this same shell.

## Page /admin
View:
    <AdminShell columnCount={6} closedWorkAccepted={false}/>

## Test: administrative navigation opens the research record
Click "#nav-research".
Expect that the text of "h2" is equal to "Claims travel with evidence.".

## Test: local question staging retains the draft and explains persistence
Type "Find a minimal counterexample" into "#research-draft".
Click "#stage-draft".
Expect that the value of "#research-draft" is equal to "Find a minimal counterexample".
Expect that the text of "#draft-status" is equal to "Draft staged in this browser only — no command was sent".

## Test: board preserves all six terminal-policy lanes
Expect that the count of ".column" is equal to 6.
Expect that the count of ".card" is equal to 2.
Expect that the text of ".closed-rule" is equal to "Closed work is terminal unless an authorized reopen command succeeds.".
